# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever happens to clone the repo.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf` on each machine decides, and a Windows checkout
# rewrites every file to CRLF. The next person on macOS or Linux then sees whole
# files as changed and real edits get buried in the noise. Worse for this
# project: the migration SQL files are content-addressed by drizzle-kit, so
# rewriting their line endings changes their hashes and `npm run db:check`
# starts reporting a corrupt migration history.
#
# So: LF in the repository, and LF in the working copy on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by drizzle-kit and hashed by it. Must never be touched.
src/db/migrations/**/*.sql -text
src/db/migrations/meta/*.json -text

# Scripts that must stay executable-shaped on Unix.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfile: keep it out of diffs, it is machine-written.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
